## Source-of-truth model

- `AGENTS.md` is durable repo policy: architecture guardrails,
  orchestration exceptions, delivery hygiene, and stable conventions.
- OpenSpec is operational truth: active change, current slice,
  completed-through state, blockers, apply/verify/sync/archive evidence,
  and next recommended work.
- Git is branch truth: a fresh session MUST inspect `git status --short`
  and `git branch --show-current` instead of relying on a branch name in
  this file.
- Runtime/project files are implementation truth: when `AGENTS.md`,
  OpenSpec, and code disagree, verify in the repository before acting.
- Memory is supplementary only when callable memory tools are available;
  never rely on memory as the sole source for current implementation
  state.

## Fresh session quick start

1. Read this file as durable policy.
2. Inspect `git status --short` and `git branch --show-current`.
3. Resolve the active change/slice from OpenSpec (`sdd-status` when
   available; otherwise inspect `openspec/changes/*/tasks.md` and
   `apply-progress.md`).
4. Treat OpenSpec's current active slice as authoritative over chat
   history or stale branch names.
5. Before edits, confirm whether the work belongs to an existing review
   unit or needs a new branch/work unit.
6. For non-trivial work, follow the globally installed `gentle-ai` /
   OpenSpec / SDD flow unless this file defines a repo-specific
   exception.

